<%#
# A dangerous action behind a question

The one way the super admin asks «точно?» before an action that cannot be taken back or that every operator will see: a
button that opens a small panel with the question, what will happen, the fields the action needs (a reason) and the two
answers. It is a <details>: it works without a script (the button opens it, the script only closes it with «Отмена» and
Escape and keeps a click in a table row from opening the row). The action itself is a normal form, so nothing is done
before «Да».

## Local variables:

- `key`: a short name of the action; `data-testid="confirm-<key>"` of the block and the ids inside it.
- `label`: the text of the button that opens the panel.
- `title`: the question («Обнулить ответы ИИ?»); without it the first line of `text` is the question.
- `text`: what will happen, a line or a list of lines (plain text).
- `warning`: a line that stands out (the person is the last administrator); optional.
- `url`: where the answer «Да» goes. `http_method`: :post (default), :delete, :patch.
- `submit`: the text of «Да» (default «Да, выполнить»). `tone`: :danger (default, a red answer) or :primary.
- `params`: hidden fields sent with the answer, as a hash (a list is sent as `name[]`, once for each item).
- `fields`: more fields the action needs, as HTML (`capture do ... end`); optional.
- `trigger_class`: the classes of the opening button (default: a small quiet one).
- `floating`: true for a button of a page header (the panel hangs under it on a wide screen).
- `in_form`: true inside a form that already exists (the answer is a button with `formaction`; no form of its own).
- `as_link`: true inside a form that cannot post to the address (a field of the edit form): the answer is a link that the
  Rails script sends with `http_method` (`data-method`), so there is no form of its own either.
%>
<%
  http_method = local_assigns.fetch(:http_method, :post)
  tone = local_assigns.fetch(:tone, :danger)
  lines = Array(local_assigns[:text]).compact_blank
  hidden = local_assigns.fetch(:params, {})
  title = local_assigns[:title].presence
  if title.nil?
    # No title given: the first line is the question (up to its «?»); the rest of the line is what will happen
    head, tail = lines.shift.to_s.split(/(?<=\?)\s+/, 2)
    title = head
    lines.unshift(tail) if tail.present?
  end
  title_id = "confirm-#{key}-title"
  answer_class = tone == :primary ? 'button button--small' : 'button button--small button--danger'
  open_class = local_assigns.fetch(:trigger_class, 'button button--small button--alt')
  panel = capture do
%>
    <div class="admin-ask__panel" role="group" aria-labelledby="<%= title_id %>">
      <p class="admin-ask__title" id="<%= title_id %>"><%= title %></p>
      <% lines.each do |line| %>
        <p class="admin-ask__text"><%= line %></p>
      <% end %>
      <% if local_assigns[:warning].present? %>
        <p class="admin-ask__warning" role="note"><%= local_assigns[:warning] %></p>
      <% end %>
      <% if local_assigns[:fields].present? %>
        <div class="admin-ask__fields"><%= local_assigns[:fields] %></div>
      <% end %>
      <div class="admin-ask__actions">
        <% if local_assigns[:as_link] %>
          <%= link_to local_assigns.fetch(:submit, t('super_admin.confirm.yes')), url, method: http_method, rel: 'nofollow', class: answer_class %>
        <% elsif local_assigns[:in_form] %>
          <button type="submit" formaction="<%= url %>" formmethod="post" class="<%= answer_class %>"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:submit, t('super_admin.confirm.yes')) %></button>
        <% else %>
          <button type="submit" class="<%= answer_class %>"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:submit, t('super_admin.confirm.yes')) %></button>
        <% end %>
        <button type="button" class="button button--small button--alt" data-confirm-close><%= t('super_admin.confirm.cancel') %></button>
      </div>
    </div>
<% end %>

<details class="admin-ask<%= ' admin-ask--floating' if local_assigns[:floating] %>" data-testid="confirm-<%= key %>">
  <summary class="<%= open_class %>"><%= label %></summary>
  <% if local_assigns[:in_form] || local_assigns[:as_link] %>
    <%= panel %>
  <% else %>
    <%= form_with url: url, method: http_method, local: true, class: 'm-0', data: { single_submit: true } do %>
      <% hidden.each do |name, value| %>
        <% if value.is_a?(Array) %>
          <% value.each do |item| %>
            <%= hidden_field_tag "#{name}[]", item, id: nil %>
          <% end %>
        <% else %>
          <%= hidden_field_tag name, value, id: nil %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      <%= panel %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</details>
